# 高频词汇 List10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List10核心词汇

{{undertake}}{/ˌʌndəˈteɪk/}{承担；从事}{The university undertook a major renovation project.}}
{{unique}}{/juˈniːk/}{独特的；唯一的}{Each culture has its own unique traditions and customs.}}
{{universal}}{/ˌjuːnɪˈvɜːsl/}{普遍的；全球的}{Education should be a universal right for all children.}}
{{update}}{/ʌpˈdeɪt/}{更新；最新消息}{The software update includes important security fixes.}}
{{urban}}{/ˈɜːbən/}{城市的；都市的}{Urban populations continue to grow rapidly.}}
{{utilize}}{/ˈjuːtɪlaɪz/}{利用；使用}{The project utilizes advanced technology to improve efficiency.}}
{{valid}}{/ˈvælɪd/}{有效的；合理的}{The argument is logically valid and well-supported.}}
{{vary}}{/ˈveəri/}{变化；不同}{Prices vary depending on the location and season.}}
{{vast}}{/vɑːst/}{广阔的；巨大的}{The internet provides access to a vast amount of information.}}
{{version}}{/ˈvɜːʃn/}{版本；说法}{The latest version of the app includes new features.}}
{{violate}}{/ˈvaɪəleɪt/}{违反；侵犯}{The company was fined for violating environmental laws.}}
{{virtual}}{/ˈvɜːtʃuəl/}{虚拟的；实质的}{Virtual meetings have become the norm since the pandemic.}}
{{visible}}{/ˈvɪzəbl/}{可见的；明显的}{The results of the program are already visible.}}
{{vital}}{/ˈvaɪtl/}{至关重要的；生命的}{Sleep is vital for both physical and mental health.}}
{{widespread}}{/ˈwaɪdspred/}{广泛的；普遍的}{There is widespread agreement on the need for reform.}}
{{witness}}{/ˈwɪtnəs/}{目击；见证}{The world witnessed an unprecedented health crisis.}}
{{yield}}{/jiːld/}{产出；屈服}{The investment yielded a 15% return over two years.}}
{{accomplish}}{/əˈkʌmplɪʃ/}{完成；实现}{The team accomplished more than expected in one year.}}
{{accurate}}{/ˈækjərət/}{精确的；准确的}{The data must be accurate and up to date.}}
{{adequate}}{/ˈædɪkwət/}{足够的；适当的}{The facilities are adequate for the number of students.}}
{{advocate}}{/ˈædvəkeɪt/}{提倡；倡导者}{She advocates for stronger environmental protections.}}
{{analyse}}{/ˈænəlaɪz/}{分析；解析}{The team analysed the survey data carefully.}}
{{anticipate}}{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}{预期；预料}{We anticipate further growth in the coming year.}}
{{apparent}}{/əˈpærənt/}{明显的；表面上的}{The cause of the failure was not immediately apparent.}}
{{appreciate}}{/əˈpriːʃieɪt/}{感激；欣赏}{I appreciate your patience during this process.}}
{{arise}}{/əˈraɪz/}{出现；产生}{New challenges may arise as the project progresses.}}
{{assert}}{/əˈsɜːt/}{断言；主张}{The report asserts that education reduces poverty.}}
{{assume}}{/əˈsjuːm/}{假设；承担}{We cannot assume that the trend will continue indefinitely.}}
{{assure}}{/əˈʃʊər/}{保证；使确信}{I can assure you that the quality meets our standards.}}
{{authentic}}{/ɔːˈθentɪk/}{真实的；正宗的}{The article provides an authentic account of the event.}}
